    "claim_boundary": "Two opposite-order pinned-core fixed-work pairs show a 5.409% median query-time improvement against allocator default for the single-partition geometry, with a 4.259% median peak-RSS cost. No confidence interval is available; the result is directional macro evidence.",
    "defensible_claim": "On the measured real DataFusion workload, compiler-directed 16 KiB Long allocations formed physically backed THP cohorts with zero runtime lifetime learning. Against allocator default, both opposite-order single-partition pairs improved query time by 5.174% to 5.644% (median 5.409%) while increasing peak RSS by a median 4.259%. The 128-group matched-placement geometry separately reduced peak RSS by 1.491%.",
    "causal_attribution_boundary": "The compiler lifetime hint selects placement; full-density THP construction and exact-key extent reuse realize the performance effect. The primary comparison uses the same compiler-instrumented binary in policy 0 and policy 9, so it supports the combined compiler-directed placement mechanism against allocator default."
  },
